# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession gathering build` from data/forever and tools/lib/professions/gathering. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/mining
title Mining 1-300
category Professions
coords era
levels 1-60
zone Ironforge

# Mining 1-300 for both factions: loops through the densest skill-up nodes for
# each skill band (expected skill-ups per yard walked), with rank training.
# A zone counts the nodes it keeps up at once (the Forever server's spawn pools,
# tools/lib/professions/gathering/node-abundance.json), not every spot a node can use.
# Skill needed per node: Copper 1, Tin and Incendicite 65, Silver and Lesser
# Bloodstone 75, Iron 125, Gold 155, Mithril 175, Truesilver and Dark Iron 230,
# Small Thorium 245, Rich Thorium 275.
#
# Spawns come from the reference data: the Era baseline (pfQuest) plus the
# node spawns Forever's beta sniffs add (Zephras Isle, the starting-area Poor
# Copper Veins and herbs: the Forever TrinityCore world DB); trainer learn skills
# and prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists; recipes and their skill colours
# from the Forever client tables (`forge data professions`).
# ASSUMED: past level 30 (the beta's cap) Forever's spawns are Classic's; nothing
# confirms them yet. In-game check: refine with Polestar_Recorder sessions.
# Ranks ask no character level: Forever's sniffed trainer lists carry none for
# Herbalism, Mining or Skinning, and level 10 for Journeyman crafting and Fishing.
# INGAME: does a gathering trainer ask a level for Expert or Artisan? (our data:
# none; one web guide: Expert 10, Artisan 25).
# Waypoints are Era-frame (`coords era`); the engine converts them where Forever
# changed a map frame, and a map without an Era frame (Zephras Isle) compiles live.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice
section Mining 1-65

step Learn Mining
  tip Any Mining trainer of your faction teaches Apprentice Mining at any level (10c), and so does the Junior Mining Trainer in each starting area; the arrow picks the nearest. Buy a Mining Pick from a trade goods or general vendor: keep it in your bags, you cannot mine without it. Turn on Find Minerals (spellbook, General tab) so veins show on the minimap. Forever's starting areas also have Poor Copper Veins (Copper Ore and Rough Stone, from skill 1). The first-hour quest of each starting area (Rascally Rodents, Coldridge Valley Mail Delivery, The Woodland Protector, Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise, A Humble Task, Marla's Last Wish) offers Mining for Dummies as a reward: reading it gives 2 skill, up to 15. Trade goods vendors and the junior trainers sell the Apprentice's Mining Pack, a four-slot bag for ore and stone (25c). If you sat at your starting area's campfire for The Great Outdoors, the camping guide there also offers Camping 101: Mining: hand it in to the mining trainer it names once you reach skill 20, for the Lodestone recipe.
  train Mining Apprentice
  buy 2901 x1 nearest

